<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mesopotamia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mesopotamian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mesopotamia is the region between and around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> rivers, mainly in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. It was the setting of the earliest cities, writing and empires, including the Akkadian, Neo-Sumerian, Babylonian and Assyrian empires. Its rich agricultural land later made it central to the Achaemenid, Seleucid, Parthian, Sasanian and Abbasid states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mesopotamia.jpg" alt="Mesopotamia" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N-Mesopotamia_and_Syria_english.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
